Teach config.sub about the substrate OS.

Without this, configure --host=i386-unknown-substrate fails at
config.sub time with "OS substrate not recognized".  The substrate
toolchain triple uses substrate as the OS field; the BFD vec is
named elf32-i386-substrate and binaries carry ELFOSABI_SUBSTRATE = 64.

Upstream substrate isn't a generally-known target, so we add it to
the wildcard OS list local to mpg123's build/config.sub copy.

--- a/build/config.sub
+++ b/build/config.sub
@@ -1754,7 +1754,7 @@ case $os in
 	     | onefs* | tirtos* | phoenix* | fuchsia* | redox* | bme* \
 	     | midnightbsd* | amdhsa* | unleashed* | emscripten* | wasi* \
 	     | nsk* | powerunix* | genode* | zvmoe* | qnx* | emx* | zephyr* \
-	     | fiwix* )
+	     | fiwix* | substrate* )
 		;;
 	# This one is extra strict with allowed versions
 	sco3.2v[4-9]* | sco5v6*)
